ops at the first block, saying why; it never pushes.\n201-`npm run cycle -- <story> auto` does the same for a single story.\n202-\n203-Three of the owner's answers are delegated, each an act recorded in the record:\n204-\n205-- **Agreement after the acceptance run.** A fresh session, which drove neither the acceptance run\ne35\n45fd8d71 docs: the comment on the default workspace exclusions wraps at 120 columns\nd5985a32 test: a protected file masked by bubblewrap fails to open with EACCES, as the comment on the mask now says\nd47587e9 fix: a bwrap in PATH that cannot be executed leaves a bubblewrap refusal citing the spawn error instead of failing the qualification with a TypeError\n27f84249 docs: the README and the verification design say Linux is supported, confined by bubblewrap and tested on arm64, and the README asks for bwrap on Linux\n0f7a288c fix: the Maven reference campaign takes JAVA_HOME from java_home on macOS only and lets Maven find the JDK on PATH elsewhere\n6e557d2c fix: the vitest control can create vitest 5's API token under node_modules/.vitest, so vitest runs under the sandbox on a machine that never ran it unconfined, and the token stays out of the candidate\n2b531938 feat: bubblewrap qualifies on Linux when bwrap creates its namespaces without privilege, refuses naming what bwrap said otherwise, and confines a command as Seatbelt does\n489d156c fix: the Maven quality bench primes the local repository with the site skin and the project's dependencies, so pmd and cpd qualify offline on a machine whose repository is empty\n5d6ff376 test: on Linux bubblewrap qualifies for linux-<arch> and confines writes, protected reads and the network, a bwrap that cannot create its namespaces leaves a refusal citing it, and Pi journeys run unconfined only where no backend qualifies\n168ed0d3 docs: the story e35s01 is in progress","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6486464e-72c1-46d2-9088-7885760fa31d","uuid":"7f7867c6-5363-4a90-9384-b11